<Document
  title="A universe, quite by accident."
  label="About All Hail the Cone"
  description="An independent creative universe born from surreal imagery. A serious home for impossible places, ordinary kindness and one sacred traffic cone."
>
  <h2>The pictures came first</h2>
  <p>
    All Hail the Cone began with a group of surreal, AI-generated images: a
    crowned astronaut capybara, a working banana, a pigeon executive, small
    devoted robots and an orange cone. Their strange consistency suggested more
    than a collection of pictures. They suggested a place.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is that place’s first public archive. The project is independently
    developed by <a href="https://github.com/marquezinii">marquezinii</a>. The
    original supplied artwork forms its visual foundation; the names,
    institutions and written continuity were developed for this first edition.
  </p>
  <h2>The absurd does not need permission</h2>
  <p>
    Inside this universe, nobody is surprised that a banana has a job or that a
    pigeon runs Bread Operations. The humour comes from taking these
    responsibilities seriously. Stories can be funny, warm, strange, uncertain
    and consequential at the same time.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Cone remains a traffic cone. Explaining it completely would make the
    world smaller.
  </p>
  <h2>A long horizon</h2>
  <p>
    The archive is designed to grow into stories, comics, animation, maps, games
    and community interpretations. This first edition establishes a place to
    begin, not a list of promised releases.
  </p>
  <p>
    Official continuity, tentative ideas and open experimentation each have a
    place. See the <a href="/canon">canon register</a> before adding a new truth
    to the world.
  </p>
  <h2>Made in the open</h2>
  <p>
    The website and documentation are available in the{" "}
    <a href={site.repo}>official repository</a>. Public source makes the project
    inspectable; it does not automatically grant commercial rights to its art,
    name or stories. The repository’s license and contribution guide describe
    the current terms.
  </p>
  <h2>Start wherever you like</h2>
  <p>
    Read the <a href="/lore">orientation</a>, meet the{" "}
    <a href="/characters">court</a>, wander through the{" "}
    <a href="/gallery">visual archive</a>, or find your way to the{" "}
    <a href="/community">community</a>. There is no required order.
  </p>
</Document>
